[43.15, "o", "\u001b7\u001b[1;1H\u001b[44m\u001b[97m Claude Code  |  real time 4:32  |  shown about 5x faster                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b8\u001b[32m\u25cf\u001b[0m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[0m(git add .gitignore packages/mtaala && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' fix(mtaala): let seed adopt an older copy\r\n    of a module with the same slug The 116 deploy served the pre-mtaala import of Misingi ya Nuru (UUID ids,\r\n    E...)\r\n"]
[43.5, "o", "\u001b7\u001b[1;1H\u001b[44m\u001b[97m Claude Code  |  real time 4:32  |  shown about 5x faster                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b8  \u001b[2m\u23bf  d597afb fix(mtaala): let seed adopt an older copy of a module with the same slug\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[44.0, "o", "\u001b7\u001b[1;1H\u001b[44m\u001b[97m Claude Code  |  real time 4:38  |  shown about 5x faster                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b8\u001b[32m\u25cf\u001b[0m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[0m(curl -fsS -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOOLBAR_TOKEN\" -H \"content-type: application/json\" -d\r\n    '{\"note\":\"The deploy DB still holds a pre-mtaala import of misingi-ya-nuru (UUID ids, English sw titles, /n\r\n    task);...)\r\n"]
[44.35, "o", "\u001b7\u001b[1;1H\u001b[44m\u001b[97m Claude Code  |  real time 4:38  |  shown about 5x faster                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b8  \u001b[2m\u23bf  {\"itemsOpen\":0,\"resolved\":true,\"resolvedAt\":\"2026-10-16T15:23:29.153Z\",\"resolvedBy\":{\"id\":\"01a144f1-10f1-736e-a2\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[44.85, "o", "\u001b7\u001b[1;1H\u001b[44m\u001b[97m Claude Code  |  real time 4:48  |  shown about 5x faster                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b8\u001b[97m\u001b[1m\u25cf\u001b[0m \u001b[97mI fixed the cause in commit `d597afb`, but the live site at 116.nuru.sh will keep showing the old lessons until\r\n  someone re-seeds its database with the new flag.\r\n  \r\n  **Cause.** The lesson files in the repo were already right. `sw/01-karibu.md` has the title \"Karibu Nuru!\" and\r\n  `sw/02-andika.md` uses `\\n`. The app was getting the lessons from its database, and the page response showed an\r\n  old import of \"Misingi ya Nuru\" there. That module and its lessons have random UUID ids, `sw` titles like \"1.\r\n  Welcome to Nuru!\" and the `/n` task. None of that text exists in the repo anymore.\r\n  \r\n  The seed couldn't replace it. The seed writes the module as `mod_misingi-ya-nuru`, saw that a different id already\r\n  had the `misingi-ya-nuru` slug, and skipped the whole module with a conflict. So re-seeding as it was would never\r\n  have fixed the deploy.\r\n  \r\n  **Fix** (`packages/mtaala/scripts/seed.ts`): `seed --adopt <slug>` takes over an old module with the same slug:\r\n  - It renames the old module to `<slug>--zamani--<id>` and makes it private, then seeds the module from the repo\r\n  under the original slug.\r\n  - Learners' progress moves to the new lesson with the same slug, and classes that listed the old module now list\r\n  the new one.\r\n  - The old module is deleted once it has no lessons left. An old lesson with progress and no matching lesson in the\r\n  repo is kept and reported, so no progress is lost.\r\n  - If a run stops partway, the next run finishes the takeover, with or without the flag.\r\n  \r\n  Without `--adopt`, the conflict message now names the flag. I documented it in both language sections of\r\n  `packages/mtaala/README.md`.\r\n  \r\n  **Tested** against a throwaway Postgres set up like the deploy: an old UUID module, one learner's progress on\r\n  `andika`, progress on a lesson the repo no longer has, and a class listing the module.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[51.83, "o", "\u001b7\u001b[1;1H\u001b[44m\u001b[97m Claude Code  |  real time 4:51  |  shown about 5x faster                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b8\u001b[32m~/nuru\u001b[0m $ "]
[54.83, "o", ""]
